The check is combined into one predictable branch hinted as unlikely, with the profile pointer loaded once, reducing redundant loads and improving code layout for the hot in-range path.
```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const FIT_PROFILE_MESG* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```